# Kotlin / Android Conventions

## Architecture
- Use Jetpack Compose for UI. ViewModels hold state; repositories handle data access.
- Offline-first via PowerSync + Supabase. Local SQLite is source of truth during connectivity drops; sync on reconnect.
- Never inline hardware access in screen/view code — import from `bridges/android/`.

## CameraX (QR Scanning)
- QR scanning lives in `bridges/android/qr-scanner/`, exposed as a composable wrapper or Activity result contract.
- Decode payload format: `gtr://part/{OEM}?batch={BATCH}` — pass decoded OEM part number back to shared UI layer.
- No ZXing/HTML5/browser-based scanners.

## Bluetooth Printing (ESC/POS)
- Print jobs route through `bridges/android/escpos-printer/`.
- Receiving clerk triggers print from management app after stock receipt QR generation.

## Sync Rules
- Conflict resolution: server-wins for financial data, last-write-wins for non-critical UI preferences.
- Queue mutations locally when offline; replay in FIFO order on reconnect.
- Never cache service_role keys in the app — use anon key + RLS.

## Testing
- Unit tests for ViewModels and repositories.
- Instrumented tests for bridge modules (camera, printer).
- Use `./gradlew :app:testDebugUnitTest` before marking work done.
